From: Lukasz Madej <l.madej@grinn-global.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Jun 2026 00:00:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bootctrl: resolve misc device by GPT label

The misc device path was hardcoded to a partition number, which broke
whenever the partition layout changed. The path is now resolved by the
GPT partition label, so it stays correct regardless of the partition
number. The label is provided by udev (60-persistent-storage.rules) as
/dev/disk/by-partlabel/misc. If the label is missing, open() fails with
the existing error instead of writing to a wrong partition.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz Madej <l.madej@grinn-global.com>
---
 bootctrl.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bootctrl.c b/bootctrl.c
--- a/bootctrl.c
+++ b/bootctrl.c
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 #define MISC_BOOT_CONTROL_VERSION 2
 #define COMMAND_LINE_SIZE 2048

-static const char *misc_device = "/dev/mmcblk0p15";
+static const char *misc_device = "/dev/disk/by-partlabel/misc";
 static const size_t SYNA_SPACE_OFFSET_IN_MISC = 4 * 1024;
 static const int kActiveSlotPriority = 8;
 static const int kOtherSlotPriority = 3;
